  "description": "Interop between NumSharp NDArray and ML.NET (Microsoft.ML) data. Expose an NDArray to an ML.NET pipeline as an IDataView over the very same unmanaged buffer (no row-by-row POCO fill, no copy — read lazily through the array's strides), read a transformer's output column back as an NDArray, and convert to/from ML.NET's VBuffer vector primitive. Conversion library only: no engine backend, no ModuleInitializer, no native dependency — depends on the standalone Microsoft.ML.DataView contract package (2.0.0 or later) and on NumSharp.Interop.OnnxRuntime for post-processing (Softmax, Argmax, TopK), and composes with whatever Microsoft.ML (MLContext, trainers, transforms) you already reference.",
